  "rhythm": "2026-09-29 redo for Poodleskirt (like So Fresh: main parts clear, solid tight drums). Songsterr s401756 (110 BPM), bars 2-10: the slap bass line note for note with its rests kept as REST, and the keyboard-trumpet stabs (top voice) in the two bars where the bass drops out. Onset to onset on the sixteenth grid; the last E held one beat. 36 beats at 110 = 19.6 s; shortest note a sixteenth, 0.136 s, so no slow-down. Drums: 'seinfeld' in songs/drums.json, kick on 1 and 3 and snare on 2 and 4 (s3907924's drum track) under the original's mouth-noise percussion pattern (s401756: shaker sixteenths, tambourine, bongos, conga), a closed hat on the one sixteenth the shaker skips so every ocarina note lands on a hit; one bar of drums first. Bass (Poodleskirt, 2026-09-29): the slap-bass track itself (s401756 bars 2-10) under the ocarina, note for note, down 4 semitones like the ocarina (same key) and one octave above the original register for stream speakers, on the Slap Bass 1 program; rendered into the drums' MIDI so it runs on the drums' beat clock. The ocarina plays this same line three octaves higher (apart from the trumpet answers and the notes folded to fit), so the two lock together. || 2026-10-03 (Poodleskirt: better than the OoT sound font version): soundfont pinned to GeneralUser-GS.sf2 so it keeps the pre-switch General MIDI band instead of following the 2026-09-30 OoT-font default.",
